    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="35.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 35.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="35.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="338" ed="#liebermann"/>Witodlice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.3-2"/>, se ðe freondleasan ⁊ feorran cumenan wyrsan dom demeð þonne his geferan, he dereð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.4-2"/> him sylfum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="35.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="338" ed="#liebermann"/>Witodlice, se ðe freondleasan ⁊ feorran cumenan wyrsan dóm demeð ðonne his geferan, he derað him sylfum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="35.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="338" ed="#liebermann"/>Witodlice, se ðe freondleasan ⁊ feorran cumenan wyrsan dom demeð þonne his geferan, he derað hym sylfu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="35.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="339" ed="#liebermann"/>Scienter, qui amicis destituto uel extraneo deterius iudicium iudicat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.5-2"/> quam socio suo, se ipsum ledit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="35.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="339" ed="#liebermann"/>Certe dico uobis, si quis extraneo aut peregrino de longe uenienti aliud iudicium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.4-3"/> iudicauerit, sibi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.5-3"/> ipsi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.4-3"/> nocet.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.6"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="35.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="339" ed="#liebermann"/>Certe quicunque alienigene uel amicis carenti peius iudicium quam suo socio (sodali) iudicauerit, sibimet ipsi nocet.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="35.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="194" ed="#robertson"/>Witodlice, se ðe freondleasan ⁊ feorran cumenan wyrsan dóm demeð ðonne his geferan, he derað him sylfum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="274" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Witodlice, se ðe freondleasan and feorrancumenan wyrsan dom demeð þonne his geferan, he dereð him sylfum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="338" ed="#liebermann"/>Wahrlich<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_35-1.lnote.de.1"/>, wer einem Sippenlosen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_35-1.lnote.de.2"/> und fernher<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_35-1.lnote.de.3"/> Gekommenen schlimmeres Urtheil zuerkennt als seinem Genossen, der schädigt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_35-1.lnote.de.4"/> sich selbst.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Truly, whoever gives a worse judgment to a man without kin and one come from afar than to his own fellow harms himself.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="195" ed="#robertson"/>Verily, he who pronounces a more severe judgment upon one who is friendless or come from afar than upon one of his own acquaintances injures himself.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="467" ed="#whitelock"/>Assuredly, he who pronounces a worse judgment on a friendless man or a stranger from a distance than on his own fellows, injures himself.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="275" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Truly, whoever hands down a more severe sentence on the friendless or those come from afar than upon his own companions does injury to himself.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="338"><ref target="clause:Af_El-to-33">Af El 33</ref>; <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-47">Af El 47</ref>; <ref target="clause:ICn_5-2a">I Cn 5.2a</ref>; <ref target="clause:ICn_5-2c">I Cn 5.2c</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. Af El 33. 47 I Cn. 5, 2a. c</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares Af El. 33, 47; I Cn 5.2a–c.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 339, October 2026 (MS Cons); AU: corrected against Rabin p. 274 / 275, October 2026 (was “ðefreondleasan”, now “ðe freondleasan”)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">socio <hi rend="italic">Hk;</hi> sod. <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">socio Hk; sod. Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sibi iudicabit <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sibi iudicabit Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-cauerit <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-cauerit K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">338</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lic <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lic Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">338</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">deraþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">deraþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.4-3" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.5-3" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i. s. <hi rend="italic">Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i. s. Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_35-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">noceat <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">noceat Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_35-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Aus Inst benutzt durch Ps Cn for 13, 1.—<hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gerechtigkeit 2d. 6. Der Zusatz I's <hi rend="italic">dico vobis</hi> erklärt sich aus der theolog. Formel <hi rend="italic">Amen dico vobis</hi>, die öfter mit <hi rend="italic">witodlice</hi> übs. wird</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used from Inst by Ps Cn for 13, 1. — <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gerechtigkeit 2d. 6. I’s addition <hi rend="italic">dico vobis</hi> is explained by the theological formula <hi rend="italic">Amen dico vobis</hi>, which is often translated by <hi rend="italic">witodlice</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_35-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 35²·³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 35²·³</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_35-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 35²·³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 35²·³</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_35-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">B A geben jüngere Konjug.-Form; <hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi> S. 38 Sp. 3.—<hi rend="italic">Vgl</hi>. Einl. 19</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B A give a later form of the conjugation; <hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi> p. 38 col. 3. — <hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> Introduction 19</seg></note>
      </div>
